          "title": "Hood Tool",
          "slug": "hood-tool",
          "order": 6,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 4089,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "\r\n\r\n\r\nSandwiched Cardigan Collar\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Knit the neckline (shaped or cut 'n sew)</li>\r\n<li>Join the shoulders</li><br>\r\n<li>Hold the neckline up to the needlebed to establish the size of the collar</li>\r\n<li>Full Needle Rib Cast on that number of needles</li>\r\n<li>Knit the collar grading it if desired</li><br>\r\n<li>Set the carriage for tubular knitting</li>\r\n<li>Set tensions -2 numbers (tighter than garment tension)</li>\r\n<li>knit 12 rows (6 rounds) grading until you have reached the garment tension</li>\r\n<li>Do not cut the yarn</li><br>\r\n<li>Set the main bed carriage to slip (Brother KC buttons in - Silver Side levers)</li>\r\n<li>With scrap yarn, knitting only on the ribber, scrap off the ribber stitches</li>\r\n<li>Lay the sweater with the public (right) side facing, on top of the needlebed with the neckline facing</li>\r\n<li>Push the neck edge onto the gatepegs</li>\r\n<li>Push the main bed needles through the knitting</li>\r\n<li>Unhook the knitting from the gate pegs</li>\r\n<li>Hang the ribber stitches in the hooks of the needles</li>\r\n<li>If desired, remove the waste yarn to confirm all stitches are picked up</li><br>\r\n<li>Closing the latches, carefully pull the stitches in the hooks through the knitting, forming LONG stitches</li>\r\n<li>Pull stitch-through-stitch to bind off</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<img src=\"/challenge/Images/v2/77/9.jpg\">\r\n\r\n\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 6208,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "imageGallery",
              "slides": [
                {
                  "src": "/v2/77/1.jpg",
                  "caption": "Full needle rib collar, \"sandwiched\"  to enclose the shaped or cut 'n sew neckline"
                },
                {
                  "src": "/v2/77/1b.jpg",
                  "caption": "Hold up the neckline to the needlebed to establish the number of needles needed for the collar"
                },
                {
                  "src": "/v2/77/2.jpg",
                  "caption": "Knit the collar the desired length in full needle Rib"
                },
                {
                  "src": "/v2/77/3.jpg",
                  "caption": "Form the \"sandwich\" by knitting circular (tubular) for 6 rows (12 passes of the carriage)"
                },
                {
                  "src": "/v2/77/scrap_off_gif.gif",
                  "caption": "Scrap off the ribber stitches only"
                },
                {
                  "src": "/v2/77/4.jpg",
                  "caption": "Lay the sweater on top of the needlebed\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Right (public) side up</li>\r\n<li>Neck edge facing you</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nPoke the gate pegs through the knitting"
                },
                {
                  "src": "/v2/77/pull_thru_gif.gif",
                  "caption": "Pull the main bed needles through the neck edge."
                },
                {
                  "src": "/v2/77/5.jpg",
                  "caption": "Pull the needles all the way through, clearing the latches.<br>\r\n*** carefully pop the knitting off the gate pegs"
                },
                {
                  "src": "/v2/77/6.jpg",
                  "caption": "Hang the ribber stitches on the needles in work.<br>\r\nRemove the waste yarn if desired"
                },
                {
                  "src": "/v2/77/pull_thru_2_gif.gif",
                  "caption": "Being careful to clear the latches, pull the ribber stitches through."
                },
                {
                  "src": "/v2/77/large_loops_gif.gif",
                  "caption": "Fold the knitting toward you, revealing the hooks and the stitches.<br>\r\nManually create large loops."
                },
                {
                  "src": "/v2/77/bind_off_gif.gif",
                  "caption": "Bind off by pulling stitch-through-stitch"
                },
                {
                  "src": "/v2/77/7.jpg",
                  "caption": "Remove the waste yarn if it's still in place"
                },
                {
                  "src": "/v2/77/8.jpg",
                  "caption": "Reveal a neat join on the public side of the knitting"
                },
                {
                  "src": "/v2/77/99.jpg",
                  "caption": "The \"sandwich\" is more noticeable on the private side along with the chain bind off.<br>Another option would be to scrap off and hand sew the stitches in place, eliminating the chain"
                },
                {
                  "src": "/v2/77/9.jpg",
